= Web server — Simple =

A web server is software or a network service that accepts Web requests and returns HTTP responses for resources it is authorized to serve.

A web server may return static representations, invoke application code, proxy requests, enforce access rules, or coordinate with databases and other services.

'''Important boundaries:'''
* web server ≠ physical machine necessarily
* web server ≠ website

